Detect strchrnul against the deployment target on macOS.

The macOS 15.4 SDK declares strchrnul with an availability of 15.4.
meson's cc.has_function('strchrnul') tests with a prototype of its own
(`char strchrnul (void);`), which carries no availability, so the test
links against libSystem and succeeds whatever MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
says. HAVE_STRCHRNUL is then set, include/qemu/cutils.h calls strchrnul
directly, and a build for macOS 14 -- Homebrew's floor, which is what
2ksbox's Mac build targets (scripts/macos-floor.sh) -- carries a weak
reference that is NULL on 14 and the first qemu_strchrnul() jumps to it.

On Darwin, ask through the real declaration (<string.h>) with
-Werror=unguarded-availability-new, so an SDK that marks it newer than
the target makes the check fail and util/cutils.c's own qemu_strchrnul
is compiled instead. Every other host keeps the check it had.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -2654,7 +2654,18 @@ config_host_data.set('HAVE_GETIFADDRS', cc.has_function('getifaddrs'))
 config_host_data.set('HAVE_GLIB_WITH_SLICE_ALLOCATOR', glib_has_gslice)
 config_host_data.set('HAVE_GLIB_WITH_ALIGNED_ALLOC', glib_has_aligned_alloc)
 config_host_data.set('HAVE_OPENPTY', cc.has_function('openpty', dependencies: util))
-config_host_data.set('HAVE_STRCHRNUL', cc.has_function('strchrnul'))
+# macOS: the SDK declares strchrnul available from 15.4, and meson's own
+# `char strchrnul(void)` prototype finds it in libSystem whatever the
+# deployment target, so a build for an older macOS would call a function
+# its floor does not have. Ask through the real declaration, with the
+# availability warning as an error, so the target decides.
+if host_os == 'darwin'
+  config_host_data.set('HAVE_STRCHRNUL',
+                       cc.has_function('strchrnul', prefix: '#include <string.h>',
+                                       args: ['-Werror=unguarded-availability-new']))
+else
+  config_host_data.set('HAVE_STRCHRNUL', cc.has_function('strchrnul'))
+endif
 config_host_data.set('HAVE_SYSTEM_FUNCTION', cc.has_function('system', prefix: '#include <stdlib.h>'))
 if rbd.found()
   config_host_data.set('HAVE_RBD_NAMESPACE_EXISTS',
